{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Joseph saw his brothers.</b> That is, he looked at them with a brotherly gaze and recognized brotherly feeling toward them; only toward them he disguised himself — hence the verse says <b>and he disguised himself toward them</b> — meaning, since they did not recognize him, they would not take offense at his speaking harshly to them, for he was to them a stranger. And he did so in order to bring Benjamin, as he revealed in the end; also to test them through the course of events as they unfolded, so as to know their thoughts toward him in that situation — and it was revealed to him that they regretted what they had done to him and counted it a sin."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:54.274202266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}